From: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
Patch-mainline: never, kabi
References: jsc#PED-16823
Subject: [PATCH] kABI fix for KVM: arm64: Maintain per-VM copy of
 implementation ID regs

Commit b4043e7cb78b ("KVM: arm64: Maintain per-VM copy of implementation
ID regs") adds the midr_el1, revidr_el1 and aidr_el1 fields to struct
kvm_arch. struct kvm_arch is embedded in struct kvm, which changes the
symbol versions of kvm_get_kvm(), kvm_get_kvm_safe(), kvm_put_kvm() and
of several VFIO exports, since vfio_main.c includes <linux/kvm_host.h>
and struct vfio_device holds a struct kvm pointer.

On arm64, KVM is built into vmlinux, and the only exported symbols
involving struct kvm are the refcounting helpers above. VFIO only passes
the struct kvm pointer back to those helpers and never accesses any of
its fields. struct kvm is always allocated by the core kernel, so the
size change is not visible to modules. Thus, simply hide the change from
kABI checks.

Signed-off-by: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/kvm_host.h
@@ -377,9 +377,11 @@ struct kvm_arch {
 #define KVM_ARM_ID_REG_NUM	(IDREG_IDX(sys_reg(3, 0, 0, 7, 7)) + 1)
 	u64 id_regs[KVM_ARM_ID_REG_NUM];
 
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 	u64 midr_el1;
 	u64 revidr_el1;
 	u64 aidr_el1;
+#endif
 	u64 ctr_el0;
 
 	/* Masks for VNCR-backed and general EL2 sysregs */
